Vendored: Lua 5.4.8
Upstream: https://www.lua.org/ftp/lua-5.4.8.tar.gz
SHA-256: 4f18ddae154e793e46eeab727c59ef1c0c0c2b744e7b94219710d76f530629ae
Licence:  MIT (see COPYRIGHT)

Files taken: src/*.c and src/*.h from the upstream tarball, except lua.c and
luac.c (standalone interpreter / bytecode compiler, not embedded).

Vendored rather than found via find_package() because a scripting runtime is
an optional, always-present dependency of the Lua scripting API (see
specs/SPEC-lua-api-v0.md section 2) and distributions do not ship a
consistent Lua 5.4 development package. The runtime is ~300 KB of C with no
external dependencies.

Local modifications: none. Keep it that way -- any patch must be listed here
with its rationale so upstream can be re-vendored cleanly.
